WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.110
- All right, let's close out

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.740
day one of our eighties celebration

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.490
with something super bright and cheery.

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:05.539
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:05.539 --> 00:00:08.091
(upbeat fun music)

00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:10.450
So y'all might remember that tie dye

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.480
saw a huge resurgence in the eighties.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.080
Designers even started incorporating

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.740
unique tie dye patterns
on runways worldwide.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.970
Now a little boy in
Pennsylvania wants to ensure

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:22.110
the trend stays as popular as ever.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:24.030
He's making and selling his own shirts,

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.710
but here's what makes him extra special.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.270
He's actually splitting the profits

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.000
with one of his favorite charities.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.150
Let's get him on the line right now.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.350
Say hi to six-year-old
Tuukka, and his mama Tiffany

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:36.090
who watch on ABC23 in Johnstown.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:36.940
What's up, y'all?

00:00:37.788 --> 00:00:38.621
- Hi.

00:00:38.621 --> 00:00:39.930
- I like your tie dye!

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:40.920
You look so good.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.101
So how'd you get so into tie dye, Tuukka?

00:00:43.101 --> 00:00:46.360
- I got a tie dye kit for my birthday.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.193
- Mm-hmm.

00:00:47.193 --> 00:00:49.680
I saw other people do it on YouTube

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.790
and it looked really cool.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:52.623
- You're like my kids.

00:00:52.623 --> 00:00:55.310
My kids are in love with
watching YouTube things.

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:56.900
So wait, tell us about your business.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.300
So how did you make it into a business?

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.530
You give some to charity, right?

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:01.400
- Yes.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.260
- [Kelly] Yeah? Do you
have fun making that?

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:04.093
- Tell her the rest, go ahead.

00:01:04.093 --> 00:01:05.410
Tell Kelly about your business.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:07.739
- I'm the CEO of Tie Dye by Tuukka.

00:01:07.739 --> 00:01:09.370
- Uh-huh.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:10.570
- I make

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:15.400
tie dye shirts, sweatshirts, hoodies

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:20.400
bandanas for dogs, baby
onesies for dogs and babies.

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:23.500
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.700
- Tell Kelly why you're
making all of these.

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:29.979
- For a $2,000 Lamborghini.

00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:31.895
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:31.895 --> 00:01:34.000
(audience clapping)

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.070
- First of all, this is news.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:38.190
You just found a $2,000 Lamborghini.

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:39.540
That's amazing.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.240
Everyone's running out trying
to find that right now.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.780
Wait, tell us about the business.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.990
So, Tiffany, what do you do with it?

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:49.109
- So I am, as he likes to call
me, his personal assistant.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:52.480
So mom and personal assistant.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:54.040
I work primarily

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.405
on keeping track of all of his orders,

00:01:56.405 --> 00:01:58.630
getting his inks together.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:00.900
I work on his Facebook group.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.245
Right now that's

00:02:02.245 --> 00:02:05.720
the main place of getting these shirts,

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.440
is his Facebook group.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.100
He is definitely the CEO.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.140
Definitely the boss.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.853
He makes all the big decisions.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:15.070
Personal assistant over here,

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:16.730
to help with whatever he needs.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:17.750
- I love that.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:19.610
Well, Tuukka, like what,
where do you give the money?

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.310
Who do you give the money to?

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:24.600
- I give the money to local charities.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.440
- Mm-hmm, and tell Kelly
who you donated to first.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:28.870
- Your Safe Haven.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.800
- Mm-hmm. Can you tell
her about Your Safe Haven?

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.421
- Oh, I love that.

00:02:32.421 --> 00:02:35.180
- They go buy gift cards
and give the money,

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:37.250
and give the gift cards

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:38.101
to moms and kids

00:02:38.101 --> 00:02:40.800
that don't have enough
money to buy groceries.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.140
- Oh, that's so kind.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.350
You have such a big heart
for such a young man.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:46.250
I love it.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:47.640
Thank you so much, Tuukka,

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.610
and thank you, Tiffany,
for joining us today.

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:51.710
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:54.020
- [Tiffany] That's right. Thank you.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.380
- All right, that's not all though.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.720
Our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of Friction,

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.670
the go-to erasable pen of
The Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.900
wanna celebrate those creating fearlessly,

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:02.770
just like you Tuukka.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.260
So they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:05.569
How's that sound?

00:03:05.569 --> 00:03:08.618
(audience cheering)

00:03:08.618 --> 00:03:09.451
Yeah!

00:03:09.451 --> 00:03:10.334
- Say, "Thank you!"

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:11.184
- Thank you!

00:03:11.184 --> 00:03:12.589
- Thank y'all, have a blessed day.

